lar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $t$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+t{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 2[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ t[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ t[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the first components, we get \n\n$$\n-4t=-16\\,⟹\\,t=4.\n$$\n\nBut then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]\\ne [\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there is no $t$ such that \n $2{a}_{1}+t{a}_{2}=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562449 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562233 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562449 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105158" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562449 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562449 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $x$, if $5a-2x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562449 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7b8162a3-2a18-5498-a3a6-ab4fdf90d980" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562449 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a-2x & =b \\\\ -2x & =b-5a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}(b-5a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]-5[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562512 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562512 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105153" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562512 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562512 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $k$, if $6{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562512 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f6e40000-d3bb-5e63-9aa5-9e060c0e21d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562512 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $k$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 6[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+k[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-6[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $k=-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562514 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562218 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562514 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105163" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562514 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562514 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562514 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f9fda870-d2c0-5b67-a720-dd733f4059b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562514 #edb/ref 1074 "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1} \\\\ 7{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $(-2)$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1} & =-9\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{1}=3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(3)+2{x}_{2} & =4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-\\frac{11}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{11}{2}$ into the third equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & =-11 \\\\ -(3)+3(-\\frac{11}{2}) & =-11 \\\\ -\\frac{33}{2} & =-8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement. \n\nSo, the system has no solution." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
